# Six that ETI Eloquence 6.1 declares and 4.3 never had, which the rules
# lifted out of it use: the cell count_input fills at the head of each pass
# of normalize_text; what kind of token was last read whole, and the two
# kinds it is compared against, a path or a host and a dictionary word,
# which set_global_constants sets to two and one; and whether a slash was
# read as per, with the one it is compared against.
short 6

# One of ours: where the number after a hyphen begins when that hyphen is one
# of a chain of them, so that the hyphen after that number is read as one of
# the chain too. hyphen_in_chain in et_numbr.up sets it and reset_sent_vars
# clears it.
long 1
name long 39 hyphen_chain_next

# Seven that 6.1 declares and 4.3 never had, which its money rules lifted into
# et_numbr.up compare against: a thirteenth kind of currency, where both number
# the first eleven alike, and six kinds of dollar. set_global_constants sets
# them to 6.1's values.
short 7
